 "context": "<div data-type=\"note\" data-has-label=\"true\" id=\"fs-idp67530224\" class=\"interactive\" data-label=\"\">\n<h3 class=\"os-title\" data-type=\"title\">\n  <span class=\"os-title-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h3>\n<div class=\"os-note-body\">\n<h4 data-type=\"title\" id=\"7\" class=\"os-subtitle\">\n  <span class=\"os-subtitle-label\">Link to Learning</span>\n</h4>\n<span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-idp64415408\" data-alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\">\n<img src=\"https://openstax.org/apps/archive/20210823.155019/resources/3c189abcf279413ade1476a0f3bd2bf4d33352dc\" data-media-type=\"image/png\" alt=\"QR Code representing a URL\" width=\"120\" id=\"8\">\n</span>\n<p id=\"fs-idp268381600\">Head to this <a href=\"https://openstaxcollege.org/l/food_web\" target=\"_window\">online interactive simulator</a> to investigate food web function. In the <em data-effect=\"italics\">Interactive Labs</em> box, under <u data-effect=\"underline\">Food Web</u>, click <strong data-effect=\"bold\">Step 1</strong>. Read the instructions first, and then click <strong data-effect=\"bold\">Step 2 </strong>for additional instructions. When you are ready to create a simulation, in the upper-right corner of the <em data-effect=\"italics\">Interactive Labs</em> box, click <strong data-effect=\"bold\">OPEN SIMULATOR</strong>.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 242749,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b209e259af552d2e.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Reg Watson/ResearchGate)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows the average trophic level of the fish caught in the open North Atlantic Ocean and coastal areas between 1950 and 2000.</p>\n<p>How did the community structure of fish changed over time in open ocean and coastal areas?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 760457,
     "content_html": "There are proportionally fewer tertiary and secondary consumers in both open ocean and coastal areas. Both areas got affected equally."
    },
    {
     "id": 760458,
     "content_html": "There are proportionally  fewer tertiary and secondary consumers in both open ocean and coastal areas. Open ocean got affected more severely."
    },
    {
     "id": 760456,
     "content_html": "There are proportionally fewer primary producers and primary consumers in both open ocean and coastal areas. Both areas got affected equally."
    },
    {
     "id": 760455,
     "content_html": "There are proportionally fewer primary producers and primary consumers in both open ocean and coastal areas. Open ocean got affected more severely."
    }
   ],
